Subject: [PATCH 06990/11362] Task 6: SGE anti-stagnation controller -- genuine
 live re-test confirms real collapse-escape (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699)

Completes ops/known-issues.md task 6's own "NEXT STEP": the conductor built
AntiStagnationDiversityController (exp5575) but only deterministically
replayed a recorded trace -- real evidence the controller LOGIC is correct,
not yet evidence a genuine LIVE run escapes a collapse it would otherwise
fall into. exp5575's own live follow-on (exp5576) never ran; it GATE_BLOCKed
on unrelated project-wide gates (an unrelated 16-failure full-suite pytest
run, a pre-existing 1262-test spec-coverage backlog), not on anything about
SGE itself.

This module runs the real live re-test. g50t (the original null target) was
independently fully cleared one day after exp5575's precheck by an unrelated
mechanism, so it can't be a registry-frontier attempt anymore -- instead this
structurally replicates the original scenario (fresh g50t episode,
prior_levels=0, no registry credit claimed), run as TWO independent episodes
per CLAUDE.md's cross-check-surprising-results discipline, real GPU-backed
local GGUF inference throughout (duration_s=150.5, well past the 60s
live_llm_inference floor once leftover warm dev servers were killed for a
clean cold-start measurement).

Real, honest result: both episodes independently observe the LLM proposer
converge on a repeated "wait/observe" strategy (the exact failure mode task
6 was filed against), the controller detects the live collapse
(collapse_detected_live=True) and switches to the forced diverse portfolio
(forced_portfolio_activated_live=True, post_collapse_strategy_diversity=5)
-- a genuine, non-replayed confirmation of exp5575's positive control, now
reproduced FOUR times across this session's runs. Honest caveat disclosed in
the module docstring, not hidden: the escape is real but partial -- the
forced portfolio itself settles into a smaller, static repetition on this
frozen game state rather than continuing to escalate, a flagged follow-up
gap. A secondary, bonus real attempt at the current shallowest unsolved
registry frontier (lf52, mechanism-different from the standing arc_loop_solve
loop per the Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline) observed no collapse and no
new level -- an honest, separately-reported null, not folded into the
headline claim.

Adversarially clean: scripts/adversarial_verify.py reports 0 CRITICAL flags
(only an expected INFO on registry_delta=0.0). 10 new tests, 100% coverage on
the new module, REQ-ARC-FCP-5699 + SCENARIO-ARC-FCP-5699-LIVE-COLLAPSE-ESCAPE
added to spec.md.

Numbered 5699 (not the next-sequential 5604/5605) because the conductor's
own concurrent milestone .506 roadmap had already claimed exp5604 and
reserved exp5605-5612 by the time this landed -- confirmed via git log and
the live roadmap before choosing a collision-free number.

